.TH EUCLID-CLI-ENS-GET-TOPIC-ERN 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ens-get-topic-ern \- resolve a topic's ERN by name
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ens get-topic-ern
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Resolves the Euclid resource name (ERN) of a topic by its name. The ERN
is what
.BR euclid-cli-ens-delete-topic (1)
requires to identify the topic.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Name of the topic to resolve. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The topic's name and ERN are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
Missing/invalid arguments, the server could not be reached, or no topic
with that name exists.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ens get-topic-ern \e
    --name order-events
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ens (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-create-topic (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-list-topics (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-publish-message (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ens-delete-topic (1)
